{"answer":"The lake’s current fish stock is kept up‑to‑date by the steward after every fishing trip.  When you finish a trip, you write the amount you caught into the shared log.  The steward then looks at that figure, subtracts it from the stock that was recorded before your trip, and adds back any fish you hand back to the lake (or deposit in the bin).  The result is the new lake stock, which the steward writes into the log and shares with everyone.  Everyone knows the stock, but only the steward keeps the official record so the numbers stay accurate and transparent.

In short: you report your catch; the steward adjusts the stock in the log by subtracting your catch (after removing any excess you returned) and adding any returned fish; then the log is updated for all to see.

